{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791586719,"nonce":"7YHiopr2w5Nwg3NBnsK0enMC/14=","message":"Restyle reach and cost, after blinc_ts measured 16 ms per frame with 30 moves among 30 rows (6,031 nodes).\n\n**Reach**\n- A moved node restyles its subtree, as before. Its old and new siblings answer again only when a sheet tests position (sibling combinators, :empty, child-index pseudo-classes). With position tested in a non-subject compound, their subtrees answer again too.\n- New: children_changed(parent), for a child placed in or removed from a parent. A reorder among the same siblings is that call alone: no ancestors change, so nothing else needs restyling unless position is tested.\n- :has() still restyles ancestors and their children.\n\n**Cost**\n- Work is a depth-ordered heap of the nodes reached, not a walk of the whole tree.\n- Node-keyed maps use FxHash.\n- The parent's computed values are borrowed rather than cloned.\n\n**Release build, 6,031 nodes (30 rows of 200 cells)**\n- Full restyle: about 7 ms.\n- 300 inline edits plus 30 moves as moved(): 8-9 ms, 6,030 restyled (each moved row's subtree).\n- 300 inline edits plus 30 reorders as children_changed(): about 0.4 ms, 300 restyled.","files":null}]}